<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.11.4: Identifying the Features of a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00247</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.11.4: Identifying the Features of a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4748f5b1-509c-4960-accb-50e70d3bce6a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">For numbers 1 – 3, consider the equation \(1.5x + 4.5y = 18\).</para>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">If we graph the equation, what is the slope of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00004">The slope is \( -\frac{1}{3} \). Rearranging the equation to isolate \( y \) gives \( y=-\frac{1}{3}x\ +\ 4 \).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00005">Where does the graph intersect the \( y \)-axis?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">The graph intersects the \(y\)-axis at \( (0, 4) \). The \( 4 \) in \( y=-\frac{1}{3}x+4 \) tells us where the graph crosses the \( y \)-axis.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00007">Where does it intersect the \( x \)-axis?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00008">The graph intersects the \(x\)-axis at \((12,0)\). Substituting 0 for \(y\) in the original equation and solving for \(x\) gives \(x=12\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
